Subject: [PATCH] argus: camera: select sensor modes per capture session

The native multi-session preview creates one request per camera but its
source observers previously reused the globally selected device's sensor
mode object for every request. This also reused that device's resolution
when requesting native-sized streams.

Pass each multi-session device index into the source observer and resolve
its own sensor mode in the mode and variable-frame-rate callbacks. Derive
native output dimensions from the request's actual source mode. Keep the
UINT32_MAX sentinel path for existing single-session callers and reject
device indexes equal to the device count before dereferencing the vector.

Common explicit exposure, gain and frame-rate controls remain shared;
Argus clips these controls to the active sensor's supported ranges. This
does not synchronize cameras or provide mixed-sensor ISP tuning/NITOs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab multi-camera launcher integration]

